%N A401477 Numbers that are not the sum of at most six 5-full numbers.
%C A401477 Erdős and Ivić conjectured that every sufficiently large integer is the sum of at most r+1 r-full numbers; for r = 5 this would imply that this sequence is finite.
%C A401477 The last known term is a(6018) = 449560. There are no other terms below 10^10.
%H A401477 Leandre Jack, <a href="/A401477/b401477.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..6018</a>
%H A401477 Thomas Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/1107">Problem #1107</a>, Erdős Problems.
%H A401477 Leandre Jack, <a href="https://github.com/leandrejack-afk/erdos-computations/blob/main/e1107/README.md">Erdős Problem 1107: numbers that are not a sum of at most r + 1 r-full numbers</a>, GitHub.
